  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Vulnerable Children Affected by the Earthquake in North-West Syria through Individual Protection Assistance (IPA).</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, Child Houses aims to reduce heightened child protection risks for children affected by the earthquake in North-West Syria, focusing on the most vulnerable groups, including unaccompanied and separated children, abandoned infants, and children at risk. As part of its goal to address these concerns at the root, Child Houses will provide 500 children with individual protection assistance (IPA). This intervention consists of the following activities: 1) Case identification and registration, 2) Provision of IPA, 3) Referral for % of most vulnerable cases.</narrative>
  </description>
